v0.20.9 - AI super overhaul: aimed gun runs, formations keep combing torpedoes (FAILED test) - Currently putting all air changes on hold
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fighters aim properly: fighters now fly their own gun run, aiming at where the target will be and pointing the nose up or down at it too (the game only tilts the nose by the height a plane is chasing, so diving fighters never had the target in their sights and never fired). They may dive at up to 45 degrees while lining up a shot, and fire under the game's own rule (within 5 degrees, in gun range). A pass now ends when the fighter has flown past its target, not after a fixed 8 s (which ended Wildcat dives before they reached gun range) (ModDogfight).
* Formations keep combing torpedoes: ships turn together with a leader that is combing torpedo tracks, and hold their evasive heading for the rest of the hold time when she is done, instead of going straight back to station across the tracks (ModAAEvade).
* Fewer [FIGHTRULE] lines.
* FAILED the test, so aircraft work is on hold. Air combat needs a full rework once we understand how the game handles aircraft. Fixes from here go under v0.21 and up.


v0.20.8 - AI super overhaul: fighter rules (tested)
---------------------------------------------------
* Aircraft before ships: fighters (both sides) sent at a ship go for enemy aircraft instead while there are any in sight within 20 km, and fighters already strafing switch to air targets when they turn up. The fighter you are commanding still strafes when you order it to (ModFighterRules, EngagementAI.AttackUnit, UnitAIAir.StrafeApproach).
* At most 4 fighters on one plane: if a target already has 4 attackers, the next fighter takes the nearest other enemy plane (EngagementAI.GetBestDogfightTarget).
* [FIGHTRULE] log lines.


v0.20.7 - AI super overhaul: Wildcats attack properly (tested)
--------------------------------------------------------------
* US fighters make their passes again: a gun run could end the moment it started if the enemy was behind the fighter (always the case after a zoom climb), so Wildcats kept climbing and never attacked. A run now only ends after the target has been in front of the fighter, gives up after 20 s if it never was, and zoom climbs stop 1 km above the target (ModDogfight).
* The 600 m torpedo drop check now only works on the run in, and the astern / ahead decision no longer flickers at the edge (ModTorpRun).


v0.20.6 - AI super overhaul: fighters spread out, stuck ships separate (tested, improved in v0.20.7)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Fighters spread out: between passes, and every 12 s in a turning fight, fighters pick their target again. They no longer all chase the first enemy plane that was spotted (in the test all 24 escort Wildcats went for one Zero) (ModDogfight).
* Stuck ships separate properly: only one of two stuck ships backs off (the one further astern, or the smaller one if they are alongside); the other goes ahead, and then both turn away from each other before going back to their orders (ModAAEvade).
* [DOGFIGHT] lines now include each plane's id and the battle time.


v0.20.5 - AI super overhaul: torpedo bomber runs (tested)
---------------------------------------------------------
* No more torpedoes dropped on top of ships: a torpedo is never dropped closer than 600 m to its target. From dead astern, the game's aim could put the drop point right on top of a fast ship (ModTorpRun, UnitAIAir.TorpedoApproach).
* Getting ahead: torpedo flights that find themselves astern of their target fly round to get ahead of her beam before going in, instead of chasing her from behind. Only if they can't get ahead within 2 minutes do they attack from astern (UnitAIAir.ModTorpedoSetup).
* [TORPRUN] log lines. The [TORP] line that was written every tick (about 20,000 lines per battle) is removed; the 5-second [TORP] status line stays.


v0.20.4 - AI super overhaul: fighter manoeuvres (tested, improved in v0.20.6)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* US fighters fly boom and zoom: climb above the enemy, dive in for one pass, zoom climb away, set up again. They don't turn-fight Zeros. Under attack they break and dive away, and a wingman nearby turns in on the attacker (the Thach Weave).
* Zeros turn-fight: they stay in the turning fight, pull up into a high yo-yo instead of overshooting, and make hard climbing break turns when attacked. Their controls get heavy at high speed, so a diving Wildcat can escape.
* Against bombers both sides make slashing passes from above and to the side, then pull away from the gunners.
* Energy: diving builds speed past level top speed and climbing costs it, plus a small wobble so planes don't fly perfect lines (ModDogfight, UnitAIAir.DogfightApproach).
* [DOGFIGHT] log lines.


v0.20.3 - AI super overhaul: realistic air attack heights and bomb aim (tested)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Historical heights: aircraft enter battle at the heights real ones flew: fighters 4,500-5,500 m, dive bombers 4,000-4,500 m (push over about 2.6 km out, release 600-700 m), torpedo bombers 800-1,200 m, Bettys 4,000-5,000 m, B-17s 6,000-7,000 m. Level bombers bomb from that height. The altitude slider for your aircraft now goes up to 8,000 m (was 3,330 m) (ModAirRealism, EngagementData.CreateUnitGroup, CombatInterface.SetUnitNavigationPanel, dive bomber data files).
* Bomb aim error: every bomb now leaves the aircraft slightly off the aim instead of perfectly on it. The spread depends on how it was dropped (dive, high level, low level), the crews' nation and year (elite 1942 Japanese crews, then worse; US crews improving), and whether the ship was turning hard. Dive bombing hits drop from about 90% to historical levels, and high level bombing rarely hits a ship at sea (AmmunitionMoveBallistic.InitialiseBallistics).
* Ships see dive bombers coming from 4.5 km (was 3 km).
* [BOMBAIM] log line for every bomb.


v0.20.2 - AI super overhaul: anti-air manoeuvres, fixes (tested)
----------------------------------------------------------------
* Stuck ships back off first: a ship pressed against another ship's hull and barely moving backs straight off for 10 seconds, then goes ahead at her old speed. Works for every ship.
* Evasion keeps going through the game's short collision-avoidance turns instead of being cancelled, and formations turn together with their leader so ships don't turn into each other.
* Earlier warning: torpedo planes are noticed from 4 km once they head in (2.5 km whatever they do), and dive bombers from 3 km.
* Combing torpedo tracks: a ship that sees enemy torpedoes within 1 km that will pass close turns to run parallel to them. This comes first.
* Rudder reversal against dive bombers: when a bomber pushes over, the ship reverses her rudder so the bomber's aim (which allows for her turn) falls where she would have been, and again for the next bomber.
* More [AAEVADE] log lines.


v0.20.1 - AI super overhaul: anti-air manoeuvres (tested, improved in v0.20.2)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Ships dodge air attacks: yours and the AI's now take evasive action when aircraft start their run on them, before anything is released. Against torpedo bombers (and low-level bombers) inside 3 km they go to full speed and turn bow or stern on to comb the torpedoes, holding that heading while the torpedoes run. Against dive bombers about to push over, and high level bombers inside 4 km, they go to full speed and turn hard. Your ships only do this with their evasion toggle on, and collision avoidance comes first. Afterwards each ship goes back to her orders, formation or manual settings (ModAAEvade, UnitAI.FixedUpdate, UnitAI.UpdateUnitAI).
* [AAEVADE] log lines.


v0.20 - AI super overhaul: stuck attackers (tested)
---------------------------------------------------
* AI ships no longer circle instead of attacking: an AI leader (or a ship on her own) that is ordered to attack but hasn't closed in after a minute, for example because she keeps turning round a waypoint she can't reach, drops her waypoints and steers straight at her target for 3 minutes. Her formation follows her. She never steers straight into land or shallows: if the way is blocked, the stuck waypoint is dropped so the game plans a new path round it (ModAIMove, UnitAISea.AttackUnit).
* [AIMOVE] log lines whenever a ship is caught.


