v0.18.1 - Crews: crew numbers and losses (tested)
-------------------------------------------------
* Every ship has a crew: its historical crew size, shown as a new Men line on the hover panel. It turns orange below 90% and red below 50% (ModCrew, MobileMapObject.AppendShipInfoFromKey).
* Battle casualties: destroyed compartments, new fires and flooding kill men, with more for magazines, the bridge, engine rooms and turrets. A ship afloat keeps at least 15% of its crew (DamageableSea.DestroyCell, SetFire, FloodCompartment).
* Experience points: veterancy counts in points (+1 per real fight) with the same ranks. Crew losses take away the same share of progress towards the next rank, but never a rank.
* Port recruits: Rearm at a port refills the crew. It resets progress towards the next rank, or drops a rank if there was no progress. Top-ups of 3% or less are free (ResupplyShips.ResetAircraft).
